Z||000009||Greg Piet||12-23-1999||06:37 AM||||William said above there will some of us in 50 years still out there trying to get parts.   I find that really humorous but tru since i filled out a survey the last time at the racetrack.  they asked "What do you expect your next vehile will be?"<BR>My answer "Pontiac Fiero"<BR>they aslo asked other questions like what is my current vehicle, do i use this vehicle to drive to school/work  etc...<P>I think that if the government still allows gas cars in 50 years ill have a fiero around!<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000010||william_thorniii||12-23-1999||09:03 AM||||First of all the plastic crack comment almost made me fall out of my chair laughing.  <P>Greg,<P>You want to invest in some land in Montana... Even Electric Uncle Sam couldn't find us up there.  We can stockpile all of the Fiero's and parts that we need to keep our wonderful fix going for years to come.  Seriously though while on the topic of Gov't mandates.  Have you heard the new studies that prove Catalytic converters are WORSE for the environment?  I just heard that one myself.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
Z||000011||ChadMan||12-23-1999||09:14 AM||||That wouldn't surprise me, William - I remember reading science magazines as a little boy claiming the world was facing a new ice age, because of pollution (late 70's).  Now the same Chicken Littles are crying "global warming."<P>Selling my 86 SE was one of the dumbest things I've ever done.  Not a day goes by that I don't miss that car.  Gotta get that house so I can start looking for my next Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000012||william_thorniii||12-23-1999||10:23 AM||||Chad,<P>There is light at the end of the tunnel.  Check back with me when you get that house... I am in the process of acquiring a vehicle that might suit you.  And I haven't run this one by my fiancee, so I might be selling it shortly after I pick it up.  At least someone in the family (of course it is the woman) thinks that you have your priorities straight.  <P>A funny somewhat related story was that before I got engaged, my fiancee and I had several talks about how I thought that if I was going to spend $X on a ring, that she should spend $X on something for me.  She laughed until I gave her the ring.  The worst part is that at the very same time that I gave her the ring, I found a Fiero that to this day, I wish I could have afforded.  Not to mention that I would have still had quite a bit of $ left over after the purchase of the car to spend on performance and body mods.  DAMN diamonds are expensive.  Not to mention that they are good for nuthin and lazy... I mean when was the last time your diamond did something for you?  In a Fiero, at least it contributes to my earning potential by taking me to work and it still has time for entertainment.  What more could you ask (Monkey... don't say what you are thinking)?  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
