Z||000017||mshill||12-23-1999||02:46 PM||||William, the diamond is just the tip of the iceberg (so to speak).  Wait until after you are married.  I have been married 16 years and just now got my allowance raised to $100 every other week.  Since I spend all of my allowance on Fiero parts I have to steal money out of her purse to buy gas and lunch.  It is tough rebuilding two Fieros $100 bucks at a time.<p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 12-23-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Boxdin||12-23-1999||05:47 PM||||In all seriousness, i use my Fieros as mood altering devices. After a rough day, week or whatever, I look forward to a drive, I plan where I'm going to go,with anticipation,  and I am always in a better mood afterwords.  I enjoy working on them, even the tough stuff. Yes, Lo and behold;<P>My name is Rick and I'm a Fieroholic!<P>Happy Holidays to all of you forum nuts, I look forward to tuning in and catching the latest Fiero news daily.||||reg||6
